hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1506","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fed us horse meat and forbade us from eating donkey meat."
"1507","Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we slaughtered a horse and then we ate its meat."
"1508","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Ammar that I asked Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them), ""Is hunting the badger permissible?"" He replied, ""Yes."" Then I asked, ""Is eating it permissible?"" He replied, ""Yes."" I asked again, ""Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He replied, ""Yes."
"1509","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Ammar that I asked Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them), ""Is hunting the badger permissible?"" He replied, ""Yes."" I then asked, ""Is eating it permissible?"" He replied, ""Yes."" I then asked, ""Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He replied, ""Yes."
"1510","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lizard, so he (peace be upon him) said: ""I neither eat it nor do I declare it unlawful."
"1511","It is narrated in a similar manner from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) through another chain from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1512","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas and Khalid bin Mughira (may Allah be pleased with them) that both of them went with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) to the house of Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her). A roasted lizard was brought before the Prophet (peace be upon him). When he reached out his hand towards it, the women present in the house said: ""Tell the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about the food you intend to serve him."" Then they said to him: ""O Messenger of Allah! This is a lizard."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) withdrew his hand. I asked: ""Is it forbidden?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""No, it is not found in our land, so my nature does not incline towards it."" Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I pulled it towards myself and ate it while the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was watching."
"1513","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two dead things and two types of blood have been made lawful for us. The two dead things are: locusts and fish. And the two types of blood, I think the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: the liver and the spleen."
"1514","It is narrated from Haram bin Sa’d bin Muhaisah that Muhaisah (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about the earnings from cupping. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade him from it. He kept discussing this matter with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Feed it (the earnings) to your slave, and buy fodder with it to feed your water-drawing camel.”"
"1515","It is narrated from Haram bin Sa'd bin Muhaysah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he asked the Prophet (ﷺ) for permission to take wages for cupping, but he (ﷺ) forbade him from taking this wage. After that, he continued to ask and seek permission until the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""You may feed it (the wage) to your water-drawing camel and your slave."
"1516","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Abu Taybah (may Allah be pleased with him) performed cupping for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace be upon him) ordered that he be given one sa’ of dates, and he (peace be upon him) ordered his owners to reduce his levy."
"1517","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he was asked whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had cupping done. He replied, ""Yes! Abu Taybah (may Allah be pleased with him) performed cupping on the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Prophet gave him two sa’ (a measure), and told his owners to reduce something from his tax, and said: 'Among the best of your treatments is cupping, and Indian costus is for your children's throat pain; do not cause them pain by pressing their throats.'"
"1518","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) through one chain of transmission. Through another chain, it is narrated from Tawus. He said, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had cupping done and ordered regarding the cupper: ""Give him his wages."
"1519","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Competition is permissible only in archery, horse racing, and camel racing."
"1520","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Competition is not permissible except in horse racing and camel racing."
"1521","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) held a race between well-trained (prepared) horses."
"1522","It is narrated from Abu Tha'labah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade (the eating of) the flesh of every predatory animal with fangs."
"1523","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The flesh of every beast with fangs is forbidden."
"1524","It is narrated from Abu Tha'labah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade eating every predatory animal with fangs."
"1525","Through another chain as well, from Abu Tha'labah (may Allah be pleased with him), a narration similar to the previous hadith is reported from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"1526","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every predatory animal with fangs is forbidden."
"1527","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog for purposes other than guarding livestock or hunting, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"1528","It is narrated from Sufyan bin Abu Zuhair (may Allah be pleased with him), he says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""Whoever keeps a dog, his reward decreases by two qirats every day."" The people asked, did you hear this (yourself) from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? He replied, yes! By the Lord of this mosque, (I myself heard it)."
"1529","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs."
"1530","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that he said: ""Fish and locusts are already slaughtered (i.e., there is no need to slaughter them)."
"1531","Rafi' bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we said: O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! Tomorrow we will face the enemy and we do not have knives with us, can we slaughter with bark or skin? The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whatever causes the blood to flow and Allah's name is mentioned upon it at the time of slaughter, eat of it. But (the instrument that causes the blood to flow) should not be a tooth or a nail, because the tooth is a bone of a human and the nail is the knife of the Abyssinians."
"1532","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Sa’d, the freed slave of Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""The Arabs who are Christians are not among the People of the Book, and the animals they slaughter are not lawful for us, and I will not leave them until they accept Islam or I will strike their necks."
"1533","Sa’d al-Falaha, the freed slave of ‘Umar, or Ibn Sa’d al-Falaha narrates that ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “The Arabs are not among the People of the Book Christians; the animals they slaughter are not lawful for us, and I will not leave them until they accept Islam or I fight them.”"
"1534","It is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""Do not eat the animals slaughtered by the Christians of Banu Taghlib, because they have not adhered to any aspect of their religion except drinking wine."" (That is, they have abandoned the rest of its practices.)"
"1535","It is narrated from Ubaidah Salmani (may Allah have mercy on him) that he stated: Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Do not eat the animals slaughtered by the Arab Christians of Banu Taghlib, because they have not practiced anything from Christianity or their religion except drinking wine."
"1536","It is narrated from Ikrimah, may Allah have mercy on him, that Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, was asked about the animals slaughtered by the Christians of Arabia. He spoke about their permissibility and recited this verse: ""Whoever among you takes them as friends, then surely he is one of them."" (__QUR_N__ Al-Ma'idah: 51) However, our teacher did not mention Ikrimah as an intermediary, and it is not established that Thawri, may Allah have mercy on him, met Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both."
